# Testing

## IRC / bot integration

- Use `TestBotBuilder` in `crates/core/tests/common/test_bot.rs`
- Handlers are generic over `Transport` + `LoginCredentials` for fake transports
- Integration tests live in `crates/core/tests/` and `crates/twitch-1337/tests/`

## HTTP / aviation

- Use `wiremock` for external API boundaries
- Flight tracker tests in `crates/core/tests/flight_tracker.rs`

## Web routes

- Route tests in `crates/web/tests/` with helpers in `tests/helpers/mod.rs`
- `dev-login` feature for auth bypass in tests

## E2e

- `cargo nextest run -p twitch-1337-web --features e2e` (or `just e2e`)
- Requires chromedriver + version-matched Chrome

## CI

CI `test` job runs `cargo llvm-cov nextest --workspace` (tests + lcov); e2e is a separate non-blocking job. Locally use `cargo nextest run --workspace` unless you need coverage.
